<Layout title="Experience — Shaurya Vijay Sinha" description="Work experience, live client projects, achievements, and education for Shaurya Vijay Sinha.">
  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Record</p>
      <h1>Experience</h1>
      <p class="prose">Research at a policy think tank, two years of competitive and client-facing consulting, and two live Detailed Project Report engagements — set out below in full.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Work experience</h2>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-item__period">April 2026 – Present</div>
        <div>
          <div class="timeline-item__role">Research Intern</div>
          <div class="timeline-item__org">Nation First Policy Research Centre (NFPRC)</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Published economic commentary in <em>Swarajya</em> on India's growth, industrial policy, and economic development.</li>
            <li>Built a fiscal exposure model for a proposed AI credit guarantee scheme (ADSBG), benchmarking against CGTMSE and CGSS growth trajectories; flagged a Year-1 fee-to-payout shortfall of Rs 195 Cr under base-case default assumptions.</li>
            <li>Modelled CGTMSE's guarantee exposure under flat vs risk-tiered pricing through FY30, quantifying an unpriced contingent liability gap of Rs 15.02 lakh crore — 37% of flat-rate exposure — against CAG-audited leverage data.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-item__period">August 2025 – Present</div>
        <div>
          <div class="timeline-item__role">Senior Consultant</div>
          <div class="timeline-item__org">Xavier's Consulting Club</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Competed in 15+ national and state-level consulting case competitions spanning market entry, pricing, profitability, and business strategy; achieved finalist and semi-finalist positions across multiple competitions.</li>
            <li>Designed an automated spreadsheet-based assessment and ranking model processing results for 400+ participants, integrating IMPORTRANGE, lookup, aggregation, and ranking functions to automate multi-stage scoring.</li>
            <li>Contributed to Cases Over Coffee, a national-level consulting competition, and the Annual Consulting Camp, the club's flagship event; framed competition rounds, managed strategy and editorial operations, and secured INR 40K+ in sponsorships.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-item__period">June 2024 – July 2024</div>
        <div>
          <div class="timeline-item__role">Growth &amp; User Acquisition</div>
          <div class="timeline-item__org">Krayonnz (National-Level Platform)</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Drove 800+ user onboardings within 30 days through a nationally executed acquisition strategy; coordinated with product and marketing teams.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Live projects</h2>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-item__period">August 2026 – Present</div>
        <div>
          <div class="timeline-item__role">Industrial Development &amp; Skill Development — Co-author</div>
          <div class="timeline-item__org">Confidential Client · Rubber, Chemical &amp; Polymer Sector Development</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Co-authored a Detailed Project Report spanning industry demand analysis, infrastructure planning, governance structure, and implementation roadmap for a sector-focused Centre of Excellence.</li>
            <li>Constructed a 5-year operating model forecasting revenue growth from INR 79L to INR 2.30 Cr and operating surplus from INR 2L to INR 78L, with break-even by Month 18.</li>
            <li>Diversified the revenue base across government-sponsored training, industry programmes, laboratory and testing services, and CSR — reducing single-source dependency in the model.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-item__period">July 2026 – August 2026</div>
        <div>
          <div class="timeline-item__role">Research &amp; Project Development — Co-author</div>
          <div class="timeline-item__org">Confidential Client · Government &amp; Skill Development</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Co-authored and drafted a comprehensive Detailed Project Report (DPR) for a proposed Centre of Excellence supporting livelihood restoration and skill development.</li>
            <li>Developed an INR 4 Cr pilot financial framework, including project costing, cost-per-beneficiary analysis, funding convergence, and sustainability mechanisms.</li>
            <li>Synthesised socioeconomic data covering 7,004 individuals across 1,606 households to inform the Centre of Excellence design and its initial pilot phase of 300 beneficiaries.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
